# A business call in Russian: не могли бы вы…
subtitle: "Phone a Russian supplier politely with не могли́ бы вы…, then pass on what was said: Russian keeps the speaker's own tense."
tags: ["russian","business russian","не могли бы вы","reported speech","russian phrases"]
teaches: ["phrases/on-the-phone","phrases/formal-register","grammar/reported-speech"]
thumb: "band \"Ask like a pro on the phone\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Both and the two of us in Russian: оба, двое, полтора","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/138-russian-both.cast"}

## A business call in Russian: не могли бы вы…
